> realtek alc880 (windows says so) soundchip.
> the sound output works fine, but none of the inputs,
> neither built-in mic, nor external mic.

Please elaborate what doesn't work.  The loopback from a mic input to
a speaker or a hp?  Or the recording from a mic?

In the case of recording, make sure that you turn on 'Capture' switch,
raise 'Capture Volume', and choose 'Mic' (or 'Front Mic') in 'Input'
source.


